# Packages

Python code lives in one uv workspace with one `uv.lock` at the repo root. A subdirectory package is a member of that workspace. Members do not contain their own workspace.

The root package holds dependencies used across the repo. A member holds the dependencies only it uses, and it depends on the root package when it uses the shared ones. uv installs the dependency list of the package you sync. `uv sync --package <name>` installs that member, the root package, and the dependencies each declares.

Add a member when that code needs its own dependencies, entrypoint, or deployable. Until then, leave it as a module of an existing package.

- The frontend lives in this repo with its own package manager and is not a workspace member.
- Development tools stay in the root `dev` group.
- A marketplace adapter ships in its own environment and its own lockfile.
